WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:16.882
When Zann and his friends burst out of the Hollow, Jev was trying to fend off the buzzing

2
00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:17.542
spy fly.

3
00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:19.784
"Wait, you crazy thing!"

4
00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:21.945
Jev complained as it flew at his head.

5
00:00:21.965 --> 00:00:23.386
"It's back!"

6
00:00:23.726 --> 00:00:24.467
Perda exclaimed.

7
00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:25.648
"What did it see?"

8
00:00:26.268 --> 00:00:27.829
Jev flapped his hand at the fly.

9
00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:30.111
"I don't know yet," he said.

10
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:34.126
"I hate spy flies—I didn't want it in my ear more than once."

11
00:00:35.487 --> 00:00:39.089
"Well, we're here now," Zann said, trying to hide his impatience.

12
00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:41.031
"Let's hear what it saw."

13
00:00:41.051 --> 00:00:43.713
"Fine." Jev lowered his hand.

14
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:47.596
The spy fly buzzed into his ear, burrowing deep inside.

15
00:00:47.976 --> 00:00:48.476
Jev grimaced.

16
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:50.478
"What's it showing you?"

17
00:00:50.758 --> 00:00:51.318
Gliss asked.

18
00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:54.741
Zann held his breath as he waited for the answer.

19
00:00:55.481 --> 00:00:58.724
He'd used spy flies enough to know exactly what was happening.

20
00:00:59.372 --> 00:01:01.954
The little creature had found Morb, as Jev had ordered.

21
00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:06.456
And it had recorded everything it saw and heard in its tiny brain.

22
00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:10.839
Now it was back, ready to pour that information into Jev's mind.

23
00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:12.599
Jev closed his eyes.

24
00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:16.802
"It's flying toward some huge stone castle," he reported.

25
00:01:16.822 --> 00:01:19.183
"Is it the palace in First City?"

26
00:01:19.463 --> 00:01:20.044
Gliss asked.

27
00:01:21.104 --> 00:01:24.206
"No. It's on a mountain with forest all around.

28
00:01:25.086 --> 00:01:26.567
The fly is looking in some windows."

29
00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:27.688
Jev gasped.

30
00:01:28.744 --> 00:01:30.666
"Whoa! There are trolls in there!"

31
00:01:30.686 --> 00:01:34.109
"Trolls?" Zann exchanged a look with his friends.

32
00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:37.572
It sounded as if the spy fly had found the right place!

33
00:01:38.532 --> 00:01:41.335
"Okay, now it's looking in the window at a dungeon.

34
00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.737
There are people in cells, and—hey!

35
00:01:45.078 --> 00:01:46.299
There's your grandfather, Zann!"

36
00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:48.801
"Boz?" Zann exclaimed.

37
00:01:49.161 --> 00:01:49.902
"Is he okay?"

38
00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:51.783
"Are my parents there?"

39
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:52.604
Gliss cried.

40
00:01:52.624 --> 00:01:55.066
"I don't know; I can't see them.

41
00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:57.388
But there are lots of people in the other cells.

42
00:01:58.196 --> 00:02:00.037
I think they're all Reds," Jev said.

43
00:02:00.057 --> 00:02:04.540
"Gross! The trolls are pulling leeches off Boz!"

44
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.403
"Leeches?" Zann echoed, picturing the tiny, harmless creatures from the local swamp.

45
00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.124
Jev nodded.

46
00:02:12.424 --> 00:02:13.625
"I guess that's what they are.

47
00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:16.026
I've never seen leeches like these, though.

48
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:17.907
They're huge—and blue!

49
00:02:18.608 --> 00:02:21.929
Boz is yelling at some tall, skinny guy who's watching.

50
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:22.890
Is that Morb?

51
00:02:23.871 --> 00:02:26.172
Oh wait—now the fly is going to a different window.

52
00:02:26.836 --> 00:02:28.237
The tall guy just came in.

53
00:02:28.937 --> 00:02:29.817
More trolls too.

54
00:02:30.518 --> 00:02:37.520
They're carrying a big black pot He went on, describing everything the spy fly had seen: Morb lighting

55
00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.021
the fire.

56
00:02:38.681 --> 00:02:40.222
The leeches burning to a crisp.

57
00:02:40.742 --> 00:02:42.643
Morb breathing in the blue steam.

58
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:44.483
His triumphant laugh.

59
00:02:45.484 --> 00:02:47.685
"Now Morb is leaving," Jev said.

60
00:02:47.705 --> 00:02:49.705
"No, wait—he just turned around.

61
00:02:50.126 --> 00:02:55.568
Wow! He totally blasted that black pot to smithereens, just by pointing at it!

62
00:02:56.236 --> 00:02:58.578
I didn't even see him make any friction before he did it!"

63
00:02:59.298 --> 00:03:00.539
Jev's eyes flew open.

64
00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:04.482
His usual cocky expression was gone, replaced by nervousness.

65
00:03:04.502 --> 00:03:06.883
"That's it," he said quickly.

66
00:03:06.903 --> 00:03:07.844
"There's no more."

67
00:03:07.864 --> 00:03:09.345
"Are you sure?"

68
00:03:09.685 --> 00:03:10.306
Perda asked.

69
00:03:11.286 --> 00:03:13.208
Jev shook the spy fly out of his ear.

70
00:03:13.908 --> 00:03:16.650
The creature buzzed around in a circle, and then flew off.

71
00:03:17.811 --> 00:03:20.333
"I'm sure," Jev said, his voice shaking.

72
00:03:20.353 --> 00:03:23.955
"And look, if you want any more favors, find someone else, okay?

73
00:03:24.395 --> 00:03:25.076
I'm done with this."

74
00:03:25.912 --> 00:03:27.233
"What?" Perda exclaimed.

75
00:03:27.533 --> 00:03:32.216
"But Jev "I told you we couldn't trust him," Zann put in.

76
00:03:32.896 --> 00:03:33.996
Jev shot him a glare.

77
00:03:34.016 --> 00:03:35.797
"Don't worry; I'll keep your secrets.

78
00:03:36.398 --> 00:03:36.938
But that's it.

79
00:03:37.638 --> 00:03:39.900
I'm not risking my own neck for a couple of Reds."

80
00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.521
Gliss looked hurt.

81
00:03:41.841 --> 00:03:43.221
"I thought we were friends!"

82
00:03:43.982 --> 00:03:44.682
Jev shrugged.

83
00:03:44.702 --> 00:03:47.924
"See you guys later," he muttered without meeting anyone's eye.

84
00:03:49.005 --> 00:03:53.487
He took off without another word, running a few steps and then zapping himself out of sight.

85
00:03:53.507 --> 00:03:56.133
"What a jerk," Zann muttered.

86
00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:58.134
"Forget him," Perda said.

87
00:03:58.154 --> 00:03:59.955
"Let's figure out what this means.

88
00:04:00.776 --> 00:04:02.537
Where do you think that castle could be?"

89
00:04:02.557 --> 00:04:05.139
"Mount Mystery," Darb said immediately.

90
00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:08.262
"There's an ancient stone fortress up there."

91
00:04:08.962 --> 00:04:10.723
The others stared at him in surprise.

92
00:04:10.743 --> 00:04:12.325
"How do you know that?"

93
00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.225
Zann asked.

94
00:04:13.245 --> 00:04:14.646
"I read a lot."

95
00:04:14.947 --> 00:04:15.887
Darb looked thoughtful.

96
00:04:15.907 --> 00:04:20.911
"Morb must have found some bigger leeches and figured out how to make his old method of stealing

97
00:04:20.951 --> 00:04:21.812
magic work better.

98
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.342
First the leeches suck the magic out of his prisoners.

99
00:04:26.082 --> 00:04:30.024
Then he cooks the leeches and breathes in the magic when it comes out as steam."

100
00:04:31.045 --> 00:04:31.805
Gliss shuddered.

101
00:04:31.825 --> 00:04:33.346
"That's horrible!"

102
00:04:33.366 --> 00:04:36.448
"But where would he find big blue leeches?"

103
00:04:37.028 --> 00:04:37.568
Perda said.

104
00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:39.770
Zann and Darb traded a look.

105
00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.212
"Probably the same place he got those stinging dragons," Darb said.

106
00:04:44.232 --> 00:04:46.153
"Huh?" Perda said.

107
00:04:46.173 --> 00:04:50.215
"I bet Morb got those leeches from a different world!"

108
00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:51.156
Zann said.

109
00:04:51.872 --> 00:04:53.853
"You mean like the ones your parents visited?"

110
00:04:54.154 --> 00:04:54.734
Perda asked.

111
00:04:55.475 --> 00:05:01.058
"Exactly. If Morb worked at their lab, he might have figured out how to access a wormhole."

112
00:05:01.078 --> 00:05:04.000
"But how could he—" Gliss began.

113
00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.662
"I don't know," Zann cut her off.

114
00:05:06.682 --> 00:05:08.503
"I don't have all the answers yet.

115
00:05:09.224 --> 00:05:10.265
But I know one thing.

116
00:05:10.685 --> 00:05:12.886
We've got to warn people about this."

117
00:05:13.727 --> 00:05:14.487
Darb nodded.

118
00:05:14.507 --> 00:05:17.029
"Let's go find the mayor and show her the diary.

119
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.451
She'll know how to get word to the palace."

120
00:05:20.231 --> 00:05:21.876
"Good idea," Perda agreed.

121
00:05:24.478 --> 00:05:28.620
But when they arrived at the town hall, Zann and his friends got a nasty surprise.

122
00:05:29.741 --> 00:05:30.921
The mayor was gone!

123
00:05:31.682 --> 00:05:36.184
People were frantically running around and shouting, and nobody paid any attention to the kids.

124
00:05:36.204 --> 00:05:42.388
"I guess Morb broke through the mayor's Shield spell," Perda said as they watched from behind some shrubs.

125
00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.029
"Now what?"

126
00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:45.629
Gliss' voice shook a little.

127
00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.590
Zann took a deep breath.

128
00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.072
"We have no choice.

129
00:05:50.944 --> 00:05:54.426
Tomorrow we'll have to bring Boz's diary to the palace ourselves.

130
00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:58.909
We can also tell the king and queen what we learned from the spy fly."

131
00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.132
"But how are we supposed to get all the way to First City on our own?"

132
00:06:03.492 --> 00:06:04.113
Perda asked.

133
00:06:04.973 --> 00:06:07.395
Zann noticed that Darb was looking thoughtful again.

134
00:06:07.415 --> 00:06:09.616
"What?" Zann asked him.

135
00:06:10.297 --> 00:06:11.077
Darb smiled.

136
00:06:11.097 --> 00:06:12.538
"I have an idea."
